e up for a better later trick. I trust my teammate's lead here and I should support it. My decision? Pass.\n\n\n", 'output': 'Evaluation: My teammate (Previous Player) has played a triplet with a single (888 + 3). Based on the card counting and game history, all triplets higher than 8 (9, 10, J, Q, K, A) are impossible for the Landlord to hold because those ranks are either exhausted, in my hand, or split in a way that prevents a triplet. I hold the only higher triplet (222). Therefore, the Landlord cannot beat this hand with a normal triplet combination and must use a Bomb to win the trick.\n\nReason: Since my teammate\'s hand is effectively the "nuts" (highest possible) for this category excluding bombs, playing my 222 would be a waste of my strongest control cards and would unnecessarily interfere with my teammate\'s potential to win the trick or force a bomb from the Landlord. Passing is the optimal strategic move to support the teammate.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": []}'}
